<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>&=
nbsp;</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>G=
itHub
Copilot: In KEDA:</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>&=
nbsp;</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>-
**ScaledObject** is used to scale a **Deployment** (or StatefulSet) up and =
down
based on external metrics or events. It adjusts the number of replicas of t=
he
target resource.</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>&=
nbsp;</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>-
**ScaledJob** is used to scale **Jobs**. It creates new Kubernetes Jobs (not
just pods) in response to events or metrics, and each Job runs to completio=
n.
ScaledJob is ideal for event-driven batch processing where each event should
trigger a new Job.</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>&=
nbsp;</p>

