nbsp;</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>-=
 **Pod
Identity** (in KEDA, CSI driver, etc.) refers to the mechanism by which a p=
od
authenticates to Azure using an Azure identity.</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>-
**Workload Identity** is the modern, recommended approach for pod identity =
in
Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS). It allows Kubernetes ServiceAccounts to be
mapped to Azure AD applications (managed identities) using federated
credentials.</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>&=
nbsp;</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>S=
o, when
you set `usePodIdentity: &quot;true&quot;` in your `SecretProviderClass`, y=
ou
are instructing the CSI driver to use Azure Workload Identity (if your clus=
ter
is set up for it). In current Azure terminology, **Pod Identity and Workload
Identity are effectively the same when using Workload Identity**=E2=80=94th=
e pod
authenticates as the mapped Azure identity via the ServiceAccount and feder=
ated
credential.</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>&=
nbsp;</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>*=
*Summary:**<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>=C2=A0 </span></p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>-=
 Pod
Identity is the general concept.</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>-
Workload Identity is the specific, recommended implementation in AKS.</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>-=
 Setting
`usePodIdentity: &quot;true&quot;` enables Workload Identity if configured.=
</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>&=
