<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>&=
nbsp;</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>G=
itHub
Copilot: When a PersistentVolume (PV) has the status `Phase: Released`, it
means that the PersistentVolumeClaim (PVC) that was using it has been delet=
ed,
but the PV has **not been reclaimed** by Kubernetes yet. The data on the vo=
lume
still exists, and the PV is not available for new claims until it is either
manually cleaned up or recycled, depending on its `reclaimPolicy`.</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>&=
nbsp;</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>*=
*Summary:**</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>-
`Released` means the PV is not currently bound to a PVC, but it is **not
available** for new claims until it is cleaned up.</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>-=
 To
reuse the PV, you may need to manually delete the PV or clean up the data,
depending on your storage class and reclaim policy.</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>&=
nbsp;</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>*=
*Tip:**<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>=C2=A0 </span></p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>C=
heck the
`reclaimPolicy` of your PV (`Retain`, `Recycle`, or `Delete`) to understand
what happens next. If you want to make the PV available for new claims, you=
 may
need to manually delete and recreate it, or clean up the data as required.<=
/p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>&=
nbsp;</p>

