<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>S=
pijker71:
what does activationTargetValue do?</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>&=
nbsp;</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>G=
itHub
Copilot: In KEDA, the `activationTargetValue` parameter is used to control
**when KEDA should activate scaling** for a trigger.</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>&=
nbsp;</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>*=
*What it
does:**<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>=C2=A0 </span></p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>-=
 If the
metric value (for example, the result of your SQL query) is **below**
`activationTargetValue`, KEDA will keep the deployment at the minimum repli=
ca
count (often 0).</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>-=
 When
the metric value **reaches or exceeds** `activationTargetValue`, KEDA will
start scaling up the deployment according to your scaling rules.</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>&=
nbsp;</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>*=
*In your
example:**</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>`=
``yaml</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>a=
ctivationTargetValue:
&quot;1&quot;</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>`=
``</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>K=
EDA will
only activate scaling when the result of your SQL query is **1 or more**. If
the result is less than 1, KEDA will not scale up.</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>&=
nbsp;</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>*=
*Summary:**<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>=C2=A0 </span></p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>`=
activationTargetValue`
sets the threshold for when KEDA should start scaling your deployment based=
 on
the trigger metric.</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>&=
nbsp;</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>S=
pijker71:
what does targetValue do?</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>&=
nbsp;</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>G=
itHub
Copilot: In KEDA, the `targetValue` parameter defines the **metric value at
which KEDA will scale your deployment to the desired number of replicas**.<=
/p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>&=
nbsp;</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>F=
or your
`mssql` trigger:</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>`=
``yaml</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>t=
argetValue:
&quot;1&quot;</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>`=
``</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>T=
his
means:</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>-=
 KEDA
will try to keep the average value of your metric (in this case, the result=
 of
your SQL query) **at or below 1 per replica**.</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>-=
 If the
metric exceeds 1, KEDA will scale up the number of pods.</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>-=
 If the
metric is below 1, KEDA may scale down the number of pods (but not below
`minReplicaCount`).</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>&=
nbsp;</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>*=
*Example:**<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>=C2=A0 </span></p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>I=
f your
query returns `3` and `targetValue` is `1`, KEDA will scale to 3 pods to tr=
y to
keep the average at 1 per pod.</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>&=
nbsp;</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>*=
*Summary:**<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>=C2=A0 </span></p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>`=
targetValue`
sets the metric threshold per replica that KEDA uses to determine scaling.<=
/p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>&=
nbsp;</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>S=
pijker71:
when to use scaledObject and when to use scaledJob</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>&=
nbsp;</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>G=
itHub
Copilot: **Use `ScaledObject` when:**</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>-=
 You
want to scale a **Deployment**, **StatefulSet**, or **ReplicaSet** up and d=
own
based on external metrics (like queue length, HTTP requests, etc.).</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>-=
 Your
workload is **long-running** or **stateless** and can be scaled by changing=
 the
number of replicas.</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>-=
 You
want to scale **to zero** and back up automatically.</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>&=
nbsp;</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>*=
*Use
`ScaledJob` when:**</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>-=
 You
want to run **discrete, short-lived jobs** (like processing a message or fi=
le)
in response to external events.</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>-=
 Each
event should trigger a **new Job** (Kubernetes Job resource), and the Job
should run to completion.</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>-=
 You
need **at-least-once** processing semantics and want to handle each event
independently.</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>&=
nbsp;</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>*=
*Summary:**<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>=C2=A0 </span></p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>-=
 Use
**ScaledObject** for scaling Deployments (always-on or stateless services).=
</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>-=
 Use
**ScaledJob** for event-driven, one-off, or batch processing workloads.</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>&=
nbsp;</p>

