<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>&=
nbsp;</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>S=
pijker71:
what does activationTargetValue mean?</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>&=
nbsp;</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>G=
itHub
Copilot: In KEDA, `activationTargetValue` is the **threshold value** for a
scaler metric that determines when KEDA should &quot;activate&quot; and sta=
rt
scaling your deployment above the minimum replica count (often 0).</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>&=
nbsp;</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>-=
 If the
metric (e.g., result of your SQL query) is **below** `activationTargetValue=
`,
KEDA keeps the deployment at the minimum replica count (possibly 0).</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>-=
 When
the metric **reaches or exceeds** `activationTargetValue`, KEDA will start
scaling up the deployment according to your scaling rules.</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>&=
nbsp;</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>*=
*Example:**<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>=C2=A0 </span></p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>If
`activationTargetValue: &quot;2&quot;`, KEDA will only consider scaling up =
when
the metric is 2 or higher. If the metric is less than 2, it will not scale =
up.</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>&=
nbsp;</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>*=
*Summary:**<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>=C2=A0 </span></p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>`=
activationTargetValue`
sets the threshold for when KEDA should start scaling your deployment based=
 on
the trigger metric.</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>&=
nbsp;</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>S=
pijker71:
what happens if activationTargetValue<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>=C2=
=A0 </span>is
&quot;0&quot; ?</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>&=
nbsp;</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>G=
itHub
Copilot: If you set `activationTargetValue: &quot;0&quot;` in your KEDA sca=
ler,
**KEDA will consider the trigger active as soon as the metric is greater th=
an
or equal to 0**.</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>&=
nbsp;</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>*=
*What
this means:**</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>-=
 As soon
as your metric (e.g., the result of your SQL query) is `0` or higher, KEDA =
will
&quot;activate&quot; and may scale your deployment above the minimum replica
count (including scaling up from 0 pods).</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>-=
 In
practice, this means your deployment will almost always be considered for
scaling, since most metrics will be `0` or higher.</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>&=
nbsp;</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>*=
*Summary:**<span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>=C2=A0 </span></p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>W=
ith
`activationTargetValue: &quot;0&quot;`, KEDA will not wait for any positive
metric value to start scaling; it will activate scaling as soon as the metr=
ic
is zero or more. This can prevent your deployment from ever scaling down to
zero pods, depending on your workload and metric.</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;font-family:Verdana;font-size:10.0pt' lang=3Den-US>&=
nbsp;</p>

